pumac-2014-team-12.body:
Count arrangements on $18$ labelled positions up to the $18$ rotations. A rotation by $k$ has $g=\gcd(k,18)$ cycles of length $L=18/g$; a fixed colouring is constant on cycles, so each colour uses $6/L$ cycles and $L$ must divide $6$. Rotations by $k$ with $\gcd(k,18)=g$ number $\varphi(18/g)$:

- $g=18$ ($1$ rotation): $\dfrac{18!}{(6!)^3}=17153136$ fixed colourings;
- $g=9$, $L=2$ ($1$ rotation): $\dfrac{9!}{(3!)^3}=1680$;
- $g=6$, $L=3$ ($2$ rotations): $\dfrac{6!}{(2!)^3}=90$ each;
- $g=3$, $L=6$ ($2$ rotations): $\dfrac{3!}{1}=6$ each;
- other rotations fix nothing.

$$n=\frac{17153136+1680+2\cdot90+2\cdot6}{18}=\frac{17155008}{18}=953056,$$
so the remainder mod $1000$ is $56$.

**Answer: 56**
